      "writtenOn": "2024-03-07T18:42:58Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "I now agree patchset 2 (with charge_manager_set_ceil moved) will fix the race issue. Thanks for the explanation.\n\n--- \u003e8 ---\n\nIIUC, get_state_pe(port) would return SNK_TRANSITION_SINK here whether the exit function is called by pe_snk_transition_sink_run ([code](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c;l\u003d3736)) or by pe_run ([code](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/main/common/usbc/usb_pe_drp_sm.c#857)) because when set_state calls the exit function, it hasn\u0027t updated ctx-\u003ecurrent ([code](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/common/usbc/usb_sm.c;l\u003d148)).\n\nWith patchset 2, pd_set_input_current_limit will be called only when PS_RDY is received. If AC is unplugged around this time, TC will run only after PE reaches SNK_READY. Thus, current limit won\u0027t be overwritten by PE, exiting SNK_READY.",
      "parentUuid": "d1ebadd9_26e39a0b",
